WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.524
Lesson three.

00:00:01.524 --> 00:00:03.257
Population and fitness.

00:00:03.257 --> 00:00:05.214
Evolution needs two things.

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:09.427
Many candidates, and a way to tell the good ones from the bad.

00:00:10.027 --> 00:00:12.407
We start with a population of pilots.

00:00:12.407 --> 00:00:14.840
Each one is thirty-six random numbers.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.168
In training there are fifty of them.

00:00:17.168 --> 00:00:18.843
Here are eighteen.

00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:21.980
Each pilot flies, and we score it.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.302
With random numbers, every one of them crashes.

00:00:25.302 --> 00:00:31.341
But some crash later, or closer to the pad, and that difference is all evolution needs.

00:00:31.941 --> 00:00:35.459
We keep the best half, and the rest are thrown away.

00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:39.921
The survivors decide where the next generation will be sampled.

00:00:40.521 --> 00:00:42.208
So what is the score?

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.616
Each pilot flies ten different episodes, each with its own terrain and starting push.

00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:50.068
Then we combine three things.

00:00:50.668 --> 00:00:54.024
First, the average reward from the game itself.

00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:59.876
That already rewards approaching the pad, and it punishes crashing and wasted fuel.

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:06.368
Second, a bonus of a hundred points, times the share of episodes that end in a landing.

00:01:06.368 --> 00:01:10.389
Landing is what we really want, so it's worth a lot.

00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:15.780
Third, a small speed bonus, up to thirty points, for landing quickly.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.555
It is multiplied by the landing rate, so a pilot can't earn it by crashing fast.
